The problem with darts (if you want them to enchant so that they
don't vanish that often) is that you have to build up a stack, and
that requires quite some time. Daggers, OTOH, can be used even
unenchanted without loss while the stack of daggers grows, and at
occasion you'll enchant them. Another difference is that (in my
games) there seem to be always enough daggers guaranteed, but
darts seem rare on a comparable weight scale, 4 dagger = 40 darts.
Then it's much more difficult to get stacks of equivalent darts
because there's the poisoned darts that don't stack with ordinary
ones any it seems that because of the larger amount you have to
collect the enchantment ranges of darts have a greater variance,
again more difficult to build a stack. Ordinary daggers OTOH are
easy to obtain at equal (+0) enchantment.

> +7 poisoned Darts at expert and maxed strength have
> an average damage of 33. It is better than many artifacts
> and is even better because it can be used at range.

As far as I see, darts at expert and daggers at skilled are of not
much difference WRT damage if equally enchanted; though an advantage
with darts (may be a disadvantage with lawfuls) is that you can
poison them (but if you're not poison resistant yourself that could
also be a disadvantage if the monsters throw them back at you).

Darts are a good option for healers, I don't mean to depreciate them;
but one has to consider also the drawbacks of those weapons. Finally
it depends on what options the game actually offers you.

